# Line endings: text files are LF in the repository and in every working copy, on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows checks files out with CRLF unless told otherwise (core.autocrlf), and CRLF breaks
# whatever expects LF: a shell script or a Caddyfile mounted into a Linux container, or a test that
# adds its own "\r\n" to a fixture to try Windows line endings (a fresh clone on Windows hit that
# one). With this file, a clone looks the same everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never text, whatever their bytes look like.
*.png binary
